,"value":"7.4%"},{"label":"ROCE %","value":"7.7%"},{"label":"D/E","value":"0.8x"},{"label":"Int cover","value":"3.4x"},{"label":"Receivable d","value":"5.7"},{"label":"Inventory d","value":"259.8"},{"label":"Payable d","value":"8.6"},{"label":"OPM %","value":"11.8%"}],"s":"MAGADSUGAR","sec":"Renewable Energy & Sugar","sec2":"Fast Moving Consumer Goods","sections":{"bull_bear":[{"body":"Not available","src":"concall","title":"Capital allocation"},{"body":"Industry volatility; Regulatory risks","src":"concall","title":"Risks & watch-items"},{"body":"n/a (non-concall source)","src":"concall","title":"Management quality / tone"},{"body":"Diversified revenue streams contribute to resilience","src":"concall","title":"Non-obvious takeaways"}],"business":[{"body":"Sugar and energy segments contribute to revenue","src":"concall","title":"Segment / subsidiary detail"},{"body":"| — | — | — | — |","src":"concall","title":"Challenges → beneficiaries & losers"},{"body":"- Part of the K.K. Birla Group, with the group in the sugar business for over 9 decades; Magadh Sugar & Energy itself was incorporated in 1932 and reconstituted in 2015 via a scheme of merger/demerger. Company carries a credit rating of A+.\n- Integrated operations spanning sugar, ethanol/distillery, and co-generation power across 3 plants in Bihar (Paschim Champaran, Gopalganj and Samastipur regions), positioned as a diversified, vertically-linked sugar-ethanol-power play.\n- Stable, promoter-anchored ownership: Promoters hold 61%, Individual/HUF 36%, Others (incl. NRIs) 3%; free float is 37.6% of the Rs 625 Cr market cap.","src":"deck","title":"Positioning (investor deck)"},{"body":"- [Transformative Agenda] Company has articulated a five-pillar transformation agenda — digitalisation of operations, rising capital expenditure, stronger governance, a systems-oriented \"Magadh Way of Doing Things,\" and people development — aimed at future-proofing the business and reducing dependence on individual personalities.\n- [Industry Policy] Sugarcane FRP has risen 29% (from Rs 275 to Rs 355 per quintal) without a corresponding revision in the sugar MSP (still fixed at Rs 3,100 per quintal), a structural risk to sector margins per management.\n- [Industry Policy] Bihar's State Advisory Price (SAP) for sugarcane was raised by Rs 15/quintal for the 2025-26 season to Rs 380 (early-maturing varieties) / Rs 360 (general varieties), an over 4% YoY increase.","src":"deck","title":"Notable from the deck"}],"latest_quarter":[{"body":"Not available","src":"concall","title":"Margins & cost dynamics"}],"outlook":[{"body":"Outlook: Stable; Strategy: Focus on sustainable energy and sugar production","src":"concall","title":"Guidance / outlook"},{"body":"Not available","src":"concall","title":"Order book & pipeline"},{"body":"Expansion in renewable energy segment","src":"concall","title":"Growth verticals / optionality"}]},"sources":["FY26 concall summary","structured quarterly financials","investor presentation (06-02-2026)","Walk-the-Talk commitments ledger","credit-rating action (India Ratings and Research (Ind-Ra) 08-05-2026)"],"thesis":"Magadh Sugar & Energy Limited has been upgraded to 'IND A+' with a Stable Outlook by India Ratings and Research, reflecting its improved credit profile and stable business operations. The company's diversified revenue streams from sugar and energy segments contribute to its resilience. However, the industry's volatility and regulatory risks may impact its performance.","track":{"expired_n":0,"open":[{"category":"capex_project","horizon":"by Nov-Dec 2024 (Q3FY25)","item":"Expand Narkatiaganj sugar unit crushing capacity from 7,500 TCD to 10,000 TCD, going on steam by November-December 2024.","promised":"10,000 TCD","quarter":"Q4FY24"},{"category":"capex_project","horizon":"FY25","item":"Narkatiaganj expansion carries total invested capital cost of ~Rs 141 crores and is expected to deliver EBITDA of not less than 25%.","promised":"141 INR cr","quarter":"Q4FY24"},{"category":"operational_metric","horizon":"post-commissioning FY25","item":"Narkatiaganj steam-saving measures to reduce steam consumption from ~44.7% to 34.8%.","promised":"34.8 %","quarter":"Q4FY24"},{"category":"capex_project","horizon":"FY25","item":"Convert Sidhwalia molasses-based distillery to a multi-feed (grain/maize/rice) distillery at a capital cost of ~Rs 32 crores.","promised":"32 INR cr","quarter":"Q4FY24"},{"category":"capex_project","horizon":"FY25","item":"Company plans to complete all announced capex projects (Narkatiaganj expansion and Sidhwalia multi-feed conversion) during the current financial year FY25.","promised":"","quarter":"Q4FY24"},{"category":"operational_metric","horizon":"post-commissioning","item":"With the Narkatiaganj capacity increase, crushing at that unit is expected to rise by 28% to 29%.","promised":"28-29 %","quarter":"Q4FY24"},{"category":"strategic_priority","horizon":"next season (SY24-25)","item":"Execute varietal replacement plan to replace red-rot-infested CO 238 cane with CO0118 and CO9301, keeping any single variety between 30% and 40% next season to improve recovery.","promised":"30-40 %","quarter":"Q4FY24"},{"category":"capital_allocation","horizon":"ongoing","item":"Management intends to reduce debt to gain financial flexibility and lower finance costs, freeing capital for value-creating projects.","promised":"","quarter":"Q4FY24"},{"category":"target","horizon":"post-conversion","item":"Post multi-feed conversion, Sidhwalia distillery (150 KLPD) can run up to 340 days and produce up to ~5.50 crore litres of ethanol annually.","promised":"5.50 cr litres","quarter":"Q4FY24"},{"category":"target","horizon":"few years","item":"Company sees scope to grow cane crushed from ~237 lakh quintals last season up to ~288 lakh quintals as saturation point not yet reached.","promised":"288 lakh quintals","quarter":"Q4FY24"},{"category":"strategic_priority","horizon":"next season if permitted","item":"If government grants full freedom, company intends to shift product mix back toward roughly 90% B-heavy/juice and 10% C-heavy, subject to price economics.","promised":"90/10 % mix","quarter":"Q4FY24"},{"category":"operational_metric","horizon":"ongoing","item":"Maize availability of ~1 lakh MT from Samastipur, Begusarai and Khagaria against a daily requirement of ~260 MT/day secures feedstock for the multi-feed distillery.","promised":"1 lakh MT","quarter":"Q4FY24"},{"category":"risk_flag","horizon":"ongoing","item":"New ethanol policy restricting C-molasses usage limits distillery utilisation (not more than ~3.8-3.9 cr litres vs 5.5 cr potential), the key rationale for multi-feed conversion.","promised":"3.8-3.9 cr litres","quarter":"Q4FY24"},{"category":"risk_flag","horizon":"ongoing","item":"Bihar low-land flooding and red-rot infestation of CO 238 variety are flagged risks to cane recovery, mitigated via embankments and topography-based variety selection.","promised":"","quarter":"Q4FY24"}],"open_total":14,"quarters_n":1,"revisions":[],"verdicts":[],"verdicts_total":0},"val5":[{"de":0.79,"fy":"FY26","mcap":640,"opm":11.8,"pe":10.1,"roe":7.4}],"wtt":{"credibility_grade":"N/A","expired_n":"0","guidance_hit_rate":"","guidance_n":"0","instrument_id":"13622","isin":"INE347W01011","open_commitments":"14","projects_ontime":"0","projects_slipped":"0","quarters_covered":"1","reconciled_n":"0","revisions_n":"0","risks_recurred":"0","sector":"Fast Moving Consumer Goods","summary":"Building track record — 1Q logged, no reconciled verdicts yet.","symbol":"MAGADSUGAR","theme_consistency_pct":"","tone_latest":"Confident and forward-leaning on capex delivery within FY25; management candidly owned the lower cane recovery (red-rot in CO 238) and flagged ethanol-policy and flooding constraints rather than glossing over them.","updated":"2026-07-29"}},"meta":{"co":"MAGADH SUGAR & ENERGY LTD","isin":"INE347W01011","s":"MAGADSUGAR","sector":"Fast Moving Consumer Goods"},"s":"MAGADSUGAR"}